core:
  - Use the project's import path `github.com/jonesrussell/goprowl`
  - Implement proper interface abstractions following Go best practices
  - Use uber-fx for dependency injection and application lifecycle management

dependency-injection:
  - Initialize `fx.App` in `cmd/root.go`'s `Execute()` function
  - Organize dependencies with `fx.Module`
  - Handle errors from both `fx.App` and `cobra.Command`
  - Ensure logger initialization before other dependencies
  - Use `fx.WithLogger` for consistent logging

core-dependencies:
  - `github.com/gocolly/colly/v2` for web crawling
  - `github.com/gocolly/colly/v2/debug` for debugging
  - `bleve/v2` for search engine functionality
  - `go.uber.org/zap` for structured logging
  - `github.com/prometheus/client_golang` for metrics

logging-standards:
  - Use structured logging with zap
  - Include relevant context in log fields
  - Use appropriate log levels (debug, info, warn, error)

command-structure:
  - `cmd/root.go`: Main application setup and fx integration
  - `cmd/<command>.go`: Individual command implementations with proper DI

command-documentation:
  - Each command should include:
    - Short and long descriptions
    - Example usage
    - Flag descriptions and required/optional status

command-error-handling:
  - Return errors instead of calling `os.Exit`
  - Use `fmt.Errorf` with `%w` for error wrapping
  - Include context in error messages
  - Validate flags before execution

command-testing:
  - Test flag parsing and command execution
  - Mock dependencies using interfaces
  - Include integration tests

command-metrics:
  - Track execution time and usage statistics
  - Monitor error rates
  - Include command-specific metrics

debug-mode-standards:
  - When the debug flag (-v, --verbose) is enabled:
    - Show full dependency injection logs
    - Use development logger configuration
    - Include detailed timestamps and caller information

error-handling:
  - Implement proper error handling and avoid panics
  - Use error wrapping with `fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)`

testing-quality:
  - Run code through `golangci-lint` before suggesting changes
  - Implement unit tests for all components
  - Use mockery for interface mocking

metrics-monitoring:
  - Implement Prometheus metrics for key operations
  - Use proper metric types (counter, gauge, histogram)

documentation:
  - Include godoc comments for exported types and functions
  - Maintain `README.md` with setup instructions
  - Document configuration options

custom-logger-implementation:
  - Implement a custom logger interface wrapping `zap.Logger`
  - Provide methods for Info, Error, Debug, and Fatal logging levels
  - Include context handling in logging methods
  - Ensure logger can be initialized with different configurations (development vs production)
  - Use the custom logger consistently across all components
